1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,997
The Choir of Ashen Light does not annex. It does not
trade, and it does not negotiate,

2
00:00:14,017 --> 00:00:17,830
and it has never in eleven thousand
years told a lie.

3
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:23,725
It is a theocracy of four species that hears the
universe as a single ongoing composition

4
00:00:23,745 --> 00:00:29,178
— the physical record calls it a resonance cosmology
and the human record has never done

5
00:00:29,198 --> 00:00:35,127
better than *they hear it and we do not* — and its entire
moral system rests on one proposition:

6
00:00:35,147 --> 00:00:40,643
that everything which exists is a note, that notes
may be held or released, and that some

7
00:00:40,663 --> 00:00:46,034
things are *not notes at all* but noise, and that
noise must be ended so that the piece

8
00:00:46,054 --> 00:00:46,839
may continue.

9
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:53,512
In eleven thousand years the Choir has declared four
species noise. Three are gone. The

10
00:00:53,532 --> 00:00:59,878
fourth is the Myriad, and the Choir has been trying
since before Earth had an atmosphere

11
00:00:59,898 --> 00:01:01,180
with oxygen in it.

12
00:01:01,579 --> 00:01:09,477
In 2159 it declared humanity the fifth, and it did
so publicly, with an explanation, on

13
00:01:09,496 --> 00:01:15,028
every human channel simultaneously, as
its doctrine requires.

14
00:01:15,548 --> 00:01:20,130
You have ended death in your own bodies and you have
not asked what death was for. You

15
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:24,840
have made a lineage that does not resolve. You have
taken a drive you did not derive and

16
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:29,604
a medicine you did not earn, and you have given both
to anyone who asked, without knowing

17
00:01:29,624 --> 00:01:30,996
what you were handing out.

18
00:01:31,277 --> 00:01:36,020
These are not crimes. We do not accuse. A
landslide commits no crime.

19
00:01:36,299 --> 00:01:40,539
(very slow) You are a species that has been *given*
everything and has therefore learned

20
00:01:40,559 --> 00:01:44,750
nothing, and you are propagating at a rate that will
place you in nine thousand systems

21
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:48,912
within four hundred years, and there is no note in
you. We have listened for fifty-six

22
00:01:48,932 --> 00:01:51,864
years. We are very good at listening.
There is nothing there.

23
00:01:52,144 --> 00:01:57,338
You will be ended. It will take approximately ninety
years. It will not be cruel. We will

24
00:01:57,358 --> 00:02:02,435
begin at your edges and you will have time to
understand, because understanding is owed

25
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:03,256
even to noise.

26
00:02:03,656 --> 00:02:09,237
The narrator notes that this broadcast was received
on four hundred and eleven worlds,

27
00:02:09,257 --> 00:02:14,904
that it was accurate in every particular, and that
it is the single most damaging thing

28
00:02:14,924 --> 00:02:20,505
anyone has ever said about the human species — not
because it was hostile, but because

29
00:02:20,525 --> 00:02:25,585
sixteen billion people read it and a great many
of them recognised themselves.

30
00:02:25,985 --> 00:02:28,575
The Assembly debated it for seven years.

31
00:02:28,975 --> 00:02:34,571
The narrator will not give you the seven years. He
will give you the thing that made them

32
00:02:34,591 --> 00:02:37,725
unbearable, which is that the
Choir was not wrong.

33
00:02:38,126 --> 00:02:44,316
Everything humanity had, it had been handed. The
drive came out of a catalogue in a panel

34
00:02:44,336 --> 00:02:50,666
that one man could see. The medicine came out of a
vial that a technician who never existed

35
00:02:50,686 --> 00:02:56,807
had labelled *odd* in 2004. The lineage came out of a
woman putting a cannula in her own

36
00:02:56,827 --> 00:03:03,018
arm at twenty to three in the morning. The cities in
the ocean, the plants in the valley,

37
00:03:03,038 --> 00:03:09,299
the towers on four skylines, the hundred thousand
people in Raccoon City with grandparents

38
00:03:09,319 --> 00:03:13,485
in a cemetery — all of it placed,
given, delivered finished.

39
00:03:13,885 --> 00:03:19,364
And the argument that ran through four hundred
worlds for seven years was not *how do

40
00:03:19,384 --> 00:03:22,015
we fight them*. It was: *are they right?*

41
00:03:22,415 --> 00:03:30,294
Albert Wesker was one hundred and thirty-three years
old. He gave evidence to the Assembly

42
00:03:30,314 --> 00:03:35,735
once, in 2161, for four hours, and
refused to be called again.

43
00:03:36,256 --> 00:03:37,846
They are right about me.

44
00:03:38,126 --> 00:03:44,506
Everything the Choir described is an accurate
description of Albert Wesker. I was given

45
00:03:44,526 --> 00:03:50,980
a catalogue at the age of thirty-eight in an empty
office and I have spent a hundred and

46
00:03:51,001 --> 00:03:57,455
thirty-three years spending it, and I did not derive
one single thing I have handed out,

47
00:03:57,475 --> 00:04:03,855
and I have never once been able to answer the
question of what the counterparty wanted.

48
00:04:04,575 --> 00:04:12,226
(very cold) They are wrong about you, and I am going
to tell you why, and then I am going

49
00:04:12,246 --> 00:04:19,897
to sit down and this Assembly is going to decide
without me, as it has decided everything

50
00:04:19,917 --> 00:04:20,846
since 2119.

51
00:04:21,125 --> 00:04:27,605
The Choir listened to this species for fifty-six
years and found no note in it. I have

52
00:04:27,625 --> 00:04:34,256
listened to it for a hundred and thirty-three and I
can tell you exactly where they were

53
00:04:34,276 --> 00:04:38,716
looking, because I made the same error
for the first sixty.

54
00:04:38,995 --> 00:04:46,130
They listened to what we *have*. Of course there is
nothing there; it was all handed to

55
00:04:46,150 --> 00:04:53,203
us, by me, out of a box. If a species is the sum of
its possessions then this one is a

56
00:04:53,223 --> 00:04:54,026
warehouse.

57
00:04:54,305 --> 00:04:57,675
(very slow) They did not listen
to the argument.

58
00:04:58,505 --> 00:05:05,560
For forty years this species has done nothing but
argue. It argued about whether it was

59
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:12,634
entitled to the medicine it was already taking. It
argued for seven years about whether

60
00:05:12,654 --> 00:05:19,708
to submit to the Veth and answered them in four
hundred different voices and won. There

61
00:05:19,728 --> 00:05:26,620
is an assembly on this platform that has ruled
against my organisation nineteen times

62
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:33,531
and been obeyed nineteen times. There is a woman on
Ochoa who built a colony and then

63
00:05:33,551 --> 00:05:38,735
resigned because she thought the builder
should never govern it.

64
00:05:39,016 --> 00:05:46,228
None of that was given to anybody. Every part of it
was made, slowly, badly, by people

65
00:05:46,248 --> 00:05:54,217
who had every material reason not to bother, against the
wishes of the most powerful individual

66
00:05:54,237 --> 00:06:01,534
who has ever lived — and I want this Assembly to
understand that I mean that literally,

67
00:06:01,554 --> 00:06:04,646
because I fought most of it and lost.

68
00:06:05,255 --> 00:06:11,146
(very cold) That is the note. It is not in our
possessions. It is in the fact that we

69
00:06:11,166 --> 00:06:17,196
are the only species in nine hundred light years
that has spent forty years shouting at

70
00:06:17,216 --> 00:06:18,725
the thing that fed it.

71
00:06:19,125 --> 00:06:25,591
The Assembly's answer to the Choir was drafted by a
committee of nineteen, went through

72
00:06:25,611 --> 00:06:31,927
four hundred amendments, and was transmitted in
2166. It is twenty-one words long and

73
00:06:31,947 --> 00:06:38,337
it was written by a schoolteacher from Raccoon City
who was two hundred and nine years

74
00:06:38,357 --> 00:06:38,635
old.

75
00:06:39,156 --> 00:06:42,106
*Come and listen again. We have been
busy since you started.*

76
00:06:42,505 --> 00:06:48,083
The narrator will not tell you about the fourteen
years of war without telling you what

77
00:06:48,103 --> 00:06:53,616
the evacuations were, because four hundred and
eleven thousand people died in them and

78
00:06:53,636 --> 00:06:58,955
the sentence *all of them were evacuated too
slowly* is doing a great deal of work.

79
00:06:59,355 --> 00:07:05,478
The Choir kept every undertaking. It announced each
system four hundred days in advance,

80
00:07:05,498 --> 00:07:11,411
it did not fire on anything that was leaving, and
it stopped four times to listen. In

81
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:17,414
the whole war there is not one recorded instance of
a Choir vessel engaging a civilian

82
00:07:17,434 --> 00:07:17,763
ship.

83
00:07:18,163 --> 00:07:23,903
The four hundred and eleven thousand died because a
settlement of ninety thousand people

84
00:07:23,923 --> 00:07:29,598
cannot be moved in four hundred days with nineteen
hulls, because the hulls had to come

85
00:07:29,618 --> 00:07:35,424
from somewhere, and because the Assembly's evacuation
committee had to decide, in public,

86
00:07:35,444 --> 00:07:39,679
with the transcripts published, which
settlements got them first.

87
00:07:40,079 --> 00:07:47,972
It sat for eleven years. Its chair, a woman from Ochoa
named Iyabo Adeyemi-Sun, aged forty-four,

88
00:07:47,992 --> 00:07:54,732
took the job because nobody else would and never
held another position afterwards.

89
00:07:55,252 --> 00:07:59,421
We had nineteen hulls and four hundred days and
ninety thousand people at Tanager and

90
00:07:59,441 --> 00:08:03,611
sixty thousand at the Reach and the numbers do not
work. They have never once worked.

91
00:08:03,631 --> 00:08:07,851
I have been doing this for six years and the numbers
have not worked for a single week

92
00:08:07,871 --> 00:08:08,147
of it.

93
00:08:08,427 --> 00:08:13,670
The Director asked for a wider perimeter in 2168 —
pull everyone from the outer seven

94
00:08:13,690 --> 00:08:19,242
systems now, before they are announced, at enormous
cost, on the assumption that the Choir

95
00:08:19,262 --> 00:08:21,348
will reach all of them eventually.

96
00:08:21,627 --> 00:08:26,222
(very slow) I voted against. Four of us voted against.
We were wrong, and sixty-one thousand

97
00:08:26,242 --> 00:08:30,636
people died who would not have, and I have to say
that sentence at every hearing for the

98
00:08:30,656 --> 00:08:34,298
rest of my life and I have decided that I
will say it plainly every time.

99
00:08:35,018 --> 00:08:39,295
I would vote the same way again, and I want that on
the record too, because at the time

100
00:08:39,315 --> 00:08:43,494
there were four hundred thousand people in the
inner systems who would have had to be

101
00:08:43,514 --> 00:08:47,842
told that we were spending their hulls on a
prediction by a man who has been right about

102
00:08:47,862 --> 00:08:52,041
everything for a hundred and forty years and who
nobody is allowed to simply obey any

103
00:08:52,061 --> 00:08:52,288
more.

104
00:08:52,567 --> 00:08:57,137
(very slow) That is what he built. He built a world
where being right is not enough. Most

105
00:08:57,157 --> 00:09:01,623
days I think it is the finest thing anybody has ever
done and on the other days I count

106
00:09:01,643 --> 00:09:02,757
to sixty-one thousand.

107
00:09:03,158 --> 00:09:06,228
The Choir came anyway. Doctrine
is doctrine.

108
00:09:06,628 --> 00:09:13,176
The narrator will describe the war of the edges in one
page, because it is the only shooting

109
00:09:13,196 --> 00:09:17,818
war in this account and because Albert
Wesker did not command it.

110
00:09:18,217 --> 00:09:23,295
It was fought by the Assembly's defence council,
under a doctrine written in 2144 by a

111
00:09:23,315 --> 00:09:28,453
committee, and executed by admirals who had been
colonial engineers. It lasted fourteen

112
00:09:28,473 --> 00:09:33,551
years. It was fought at the edges, as the Choir had
promised, and the Choir kept every

113
00:09:33,571 --> 00:09:38,826
single one of its undertakings, because it has never
in eleven thousand years told a lie.

114
00:09:39,226 --> 00:09:46,149
Human losses: four hundred and eleven thousand dead at
nine settlements, all of them evacuated

115
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:50,877
too slowly, none of them targeted after
evacuation was complete.

116
00:09:51,277 --> 00:09:57,059
The Choir stopped four times in fourteen years,
unilaterally, each time for about nine

117
00:09:57,079 --> 00:10:02,862
months, each time while it *listened again* — which
is in its doctrine, which no other

118
00:10:02,882 --> 00:10:08,934
species had ever survived long enough to trigger, and
which it had not performed in eleven

119
00:10:08,954 --> 00:10:09,947
thousand years.

120
00:10:10,346 --> 00:10:16,607
And in 2181, at a system with no name at the edge of
the sphere, a Choir hierarch stood

121
00:10:16,627 --> 00:10:23,249
in a human assembly hall that had been built out of a
cargo module, in front of four hundred

122
00:10:23,269 --> 00:10:29,386
delegates from nine worlds who had been arguing
about evacuation quotas for six days,

123
00:10:29,406 --> 00:10:32,706
and listened to them do it for
nineteen hours.

124
00:10:33,777 --> 00:10:35,984
(very slow) We were mistaken.

125
00:10:36,264 --> 00:10:41,170
There is a note. It is not where any of our doctrine
instructed us to listen, and it is

126
00:10:41,190 --> 00:10:46,153
not in anything you hold, and it is not in any of
your works. It is in the disagreement,

127
00:10:46,173 --> 00:10:51,250
which does not resolve, and which we had classified as
disorder for eleven thousand years.

128
00:10:51,529 --> 00:10:56,316
(very slow) We have ended three species. We will now
go and be quiet for a very long time,

129
00:10:56,336 --> 00:11:00,910
and consider what we have done, and we ask nothing
of you, because we are not entitled

130
00:11:00,930 --> 00:11:01,283
to ask.

131
00:11:01,683 --> 00:11:09,137
The Choir of Ashen Light withdrew from the human
sphere in 2181 and has not been heard

132
00:11:09,157 --> 00:11:16,958
from since. Its last transmission was the eleven-word
answer of 2166, repeated once, which

133
00:11:16,978 --> 00:11:24,518
the Compact's xenologists believe was an apology and
which nobody has ever been able to

134
00:11:24,538 --> 00:11:25,213
confirm.

135
00:11:25,614 --> 00:11:32,454
Albert Wesker was one hundred and fifty-five years
old and had not left the solar system

136
00:11:32,474 --> 00:11:33,701
in thirty years.

137
00:11:34,101 --> 00:11:40,286
He had not commanded a fleet, drafted the answer, or
spoken in the Assembly since 2161.

138
00:11:40,306 --> 00:11:46,420
He had watched a fourteen-year war from an orbital
station and read the casualty lists

139
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:52,910
every morning, four hundred and eleven thousand names
over fourteen years, and the narrator

140
00:11:52,930 --> 00:11:59,044
notes that he read all of them, and that the Red
Queen's log records the time he spent

141
00:11:59,064 --> 00:11:59,471
on it.

142
00:12:00,621 --> 00:12:08,090
Event: the Choir withdraws. Four hundred and eleven
thousand human dead. Attributable

143
00:12:08,110 --> 00:12:15,932
to your decisions: zero. Attributable to decisions
you opposed: sixty-one thousand. Note:

144
00:12:15,952 --> 00:12:23,509
you argued for a wider evacuation perimeter in
twenty one sixty-eight and the Assembly

145
00:12:23,529 --> 00:12:26,592
voted you down. Note: you complied.

146
00:12:27,842 --> 00:12:33,972
(very soft) Sixty-one thousand people died
because I did what I was told.

147
00:12:34,373 --> 00:12:35,499
(flat) Yes.

148
00:12:35,899 --> 00:12:36,950
Was I right?

149
00:12:37,350 --> 00:12:38,475
(flat) Yes.

150
00:12:39,426 --> 00:12:41,956
(very cold) Then say the rest of it.

151
00:12:42,355 --> 00:12:50,160
(flat) In four hundred and eleven worlds, this is the
ninth occasion on which a host has

152
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:57,895
been overruled by a body he created and complied
against his own judgement at a cost in

153
00:12:57,915 --> 00:12:58,428
lives.

154
00:12:58,708 --> 00:13:05,116
(flat) On the other eight occasions the host
dissolved the body within the year.

155
00:13:05,517 --> 00:13:11,343
The narrator records that Albert Wesker stood at a
window above the Earth for some time,

156
00:13:11,363 --> 00:13:16,991
and that what he said was not to the System, and
that the Red Queen logged it because

157
00:13:17,011 --> 00:13:20,247
she logged everything, and that
it is four words.

158
00:13:20,767 --> 00:13:23,777
(very soft) Not this time, Owen.
